=== SERIALIZATION ===
# Phase-42 typed envelope JSON shape:
#   {"kind": <protomodel.ValueKind int>, "v": <typed JSON value>, "ts": <unix nanos>}
#
# Encoder uses metadata-first kind inference:
#   1. Look up protomodel.SignalsByName[field].ValueKind
#   2. Fall back to runtime type switch on the Go value
#
# Decoder switches on Kind to unmarshal V into the right Go type:
#   ValueKindString/Enum -> string
#   ValueKindBool        -> bool
#   ValueKindInt32       -> int32
#   ValueKindInt64       -> int64
#   ValueKindFloat       -> float32
#   ValueKindDouble      -> float64
#   ValueKindTime        -> time.Time
#   ValueKindCompound    -> generic interface{} (map/slice)
#   ValueKindUnknown/0   -> generic interface{} (untyped)
#
# Backward-compat reads:
#   1. Typed envelope (kind+v+ts present)
#   2. Pre-phase-42 envelope (encoding+value+timestamp)
#   3. Legacy scalar (number / "true" / "false" / JSON / string)
#
# Stale-cache contract (NEW Fresh-only API):
#   * default staleAfter = LiveSignalFreshnessThreshold (2m)
#   * GetSignalValueFresh(ctx, vehicleID, name) (*Value, error)
#       returns (advisoryValue, ErrStale) for stale or legacy zero-Timestamp entries
#       increments tesla_signal_cache_stale_total{vehicle_id, field}
#   * Existing GetSignalValue/GetAllValues unchanged: silently return values to
#     preserve the immutable live_store_test.go contract that requires merged
#     map preservation of stale L2 envelopes (TestHybridLiveSignalStoreGetAll
#     ReturnsStaleL2EnvelopesWithTimestampPreserved).
#
# Constructor:
#   NewRedisSignalCache(rdb, opts ...RedisSignalCacheOption) *RedisSignalCache
#   WithStaleAfter(d time.Duration) RedisSignalCacheOption
#
# Direct-struct construction (&RedisSignalCache{rdb: x}) yields
# staleAfter = 0, which DISABLES freshness checks and preserves the
# pass-through behaviour the existing live_store_test.go relies on.

